				"readmeComment": "The start actions send the start command of the Mi Home app with the cleaning type and mode as constants; starting again after a pause resumes the run. Point cleaning: write `point-x` and `point-y` first; zone cleaning: write `zone-points` first; then send the start action. Map editing (virtual walls, restricted areas) and schedules need several inputs and are not available. Value mapping `[\"start-vacuum\"\u003d\"Start vacuuming\",\"start-vacuum-walls\"\u003d\"Start vacuuming along walls\",\"start-vacuum-mop\"\u003d\"Start vacuuming and mopping\",\"start-vacuum-mop-walls\"\u003d\"Start vacuuming and mopping along walls\",\"start-mop\"\u003d\"Start mopping\",\"start-mop-walls\"\u003d\"Start mopping along walls\",\"stop-sweeping\"\u003d\"Stop cleaning\",\"pause\"\u003d\"Pause cleaning\",\"start-charge\"\u003d\"Go to dock\",\"stop-charge\"\u003d\"Stop returning to dock\",\"find-device\"\u003d\"Locate the robot\",\"start-point-clean\"\u003d\"Start point cleaning\",\"pause-point-clean\"\u003d\"Pause point cleaning\",\"start-zone-clean\"\u003d\"Start zone cleaning\",\"pause-zone-clean\"\u003d\"Pause zone cleaning\",\"reset-map\"\u003d\"Clear the saved map\",\"set-calibration\"\u003d\"Calibrate\"]`"
			},
